  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strenthening Partnership Toward Participatory and Accountable Governance of Rural WASH in Pursat</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project&#x2019;s goal is increase access to and promote sound management of water resources for improved health of communities in Pursat, by: improving access to potable water; improving access to sustainable improved sanitation; increasing adaption of key hygiene behaviours. Predictable access to safe water and sanitation expands job opportunity for both men and women, improves food security and nutrition, and protects health and the environment. Srer Khmer&#x2019;s WASH project includes three interdependent pillars, making it a balanced and sustainable approach: (1) providing hardware (e.g. infrastructure); (2) promoting behaviour change; (3) supporting an enabling policy and institutional environment and partner capacity development. Project will be implemented in 10 villages in Sna communes in Krokor districts in most vulnerable communities. A total of 6,692 persons ( 3,314 females) will be targeted.</narrative>
  </description>
